@ajs, 2026-10-18, from his 20 years in Air Force and Space Force acquisitions: "I thought logical inference from intelligence can drive design processes. Often intelligence has some measure of uncertainty and may not be accurate. Being able to carefully and logically deduce credible intelligence from a whole slew of intelligence products and types is not easy. … Acquisition Intelligence … ensures that American weapons systems are built to defeat actual, evolving adversary capabilities rather than hypothetical ones." He walked through:
- Requirements (JFRP/JCIDS; the VOLT threat baseline written into the CDD);
- Development (Intelligence Mission Data; the LMDP levied on the Intelligence Community);
- Test and Evaluation (a TEMP whose parameters mimic the VOLT; threat emulators);
- Fielding (EWIR reprogramming feeding new signals back).
"I feel that some of our work on lines of reasoning and argumentative frameworks could properly inform design."

THE MAP onto reflow2, as recorded the same day:
- Conflicting intelligence products of varying credibility are claims with objections read the Dung way (fact:reflow2-reads-an-attack-graph-by-grounded-semantics-reinstatement-works-and-cycles-stay-undecided-unnamed-2026-10-18), with confidence recorded and corroboration kept apart from proof.
- VOLT → CDD: a requirement's reason to exist is the chain resting on the threat assessment (req:an-edge-names-the-claim-that-argues-for-it-and-a-governed-requirement-reads-its-reason-to-exist, phase 2). When the assessment changes, the requirements it governs are named.
- LMDP: a requirement levied on another design arrives proposed (req:a-requirement-reaches-a-design-its-sender-does-not-own-at-proposed-with-its-origin-and-binds-on-the-receivers-word).
- TEMP: a check whose conditions rest on threat claims goes stale when they change.
- EWIR: operations feed the design (dec:idea-reflow2-serves-a-design-in-operations-where-incidents-feed-the-design), with the intelligence in its own design (req:reasoning-crosses-designs-within-a-hub, phase 4).
- Analytic rigour (ICD 203 confidence; Heuer's Analysis of Competing Hypotheses) is competing hypotheses attacking each other: the argumentation framework, and the kept idea (e) of naming the consistent choices.

THE CAPSTONE TRIAL, after build phase 2 ("Record it; trial after phase 2"):
1. a fictional or open-source threat baseline with conflicting reports of differing credibility;
2. a threat assessment reasoned from them;
3. requirements whose reason to exist rests on that assessment;
4. a threat-based test;
5. then an "intelligence update" that defeats an old report. reflow2 must name which requirements and tests lose their reason.
Later, once phase 4 lands, the intelligence moves into its own design, as the Intelligence Community and the program office are separate.

PUSHBACK, RECORDED BESIDE IT:
- CLASSIFICATION: flo2.io is unclassified hosting, so fictional or public open-source material only, never real intelligence.
- Credibility is the analyst's judgement (the agent or a person). reflow2 records sources, confidence and attacks, and computes what follows. Numeric probabilities are mostly false precision.
- This is the payoff of build phases 1, 2 and 4 and the kept framework ideas, a use case rather than new surface (fewer things).
